  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "A role that is a standing defect and reads 'unknown' for one tick counts as clear. fileStandingDefects sends that role an ObsClear observation with ClearTicks 1, which closes the defect episode. The failure count and cause survive the unknown reading, so on the next dead reading the role stands again at once and a fresh defect notice is opened and delivered. A single unknown reading therefore produces a second notice for the same failure. Sending ObsUnknown, which the pattern lifecycle already has, would keep the episode open instead. The slice still works and is safe without this fix: at most one notice is ever open, and the repeat only happens after a real unknown reading. So under rule R-124 (a finding is material only when the slice does not work or is not safe without the fix) this is not material.",
      "evidence": "Traced causal path, no reproduction. In health.go applyHealthObservation, an unknown status hits `continue` before the count or cause is reset. standingRoles then sets Standing to false for any role that is not dead. In fileStandingDefects (health.go, around line 870) every role that is not standing gets ObsClear. In pattern_episode.go applyPatternObservation, ObsClear with CleanCount >= ClearTicks (1) marks the episode Cleared. On the next tick the dead reading has the same cause and the count is still 5, so ObsFinding finds no open episode, calls openAlertLocked, which creates a new episode, and submitEpisode delivers it.",
